				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement terminal shell integration event handling\n\nAdd handlers for `$acceptTerminalShellIntegrationActivated` and `$acceptTerminalCwdChange` notifications from Sky Bridge, enabling extensions to observe terminal shell integration state via `onDidChangeTerminalShellIntegration`.\n\nThe `$acceptTerminalShellIntegrationActivated` handler sets a minimal `shellIntegration` stub on the matching terminal when OSC 633 ; A is first seen, firing the event so extension subscriptions resolve. The `$acceptTerminalCwdChange` handler parses OSC 633 P;cwd= sequences and builds a URI-like object (with `scheme`, `path`, `fsPath`, `toString()`) matching VS Code's `vscode.Uri` shape, so extensions can read `.shellIntegration.cwd.fsPath` without special-casing.\n\nThe terminal stub in HandleSpecificNotification now initializes `shellIntegration: undefined` so extensions can guard with `?.` before access. Additionally, `setLanguageConfiguration` in the API factory now forwards the full `config` payload to Mountain instead of discarding it.\n\nExtensions such as openai.chatgpt can now observe terminal shell integration state in Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "1d20cadee215f6638f143dd3fb7d6809a9e0dd1e"
		},
